{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"buzzers","name":"Buzzers","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"An active buzzer (beeps by itself when powered) and a passive buzzer (plays the note you give it with tone()). You hear them: the toolbar's Sound button turns part sounds on and off.","category":"Sound","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// Buzzers. An active one has its own oscillator: DC on its + makes it beep at its own pitch. A\n// passive one is just a little speaker: it sounds at whatever frequency its + is switched at\n// (tone() is PWM at that frequency), and a steady level only clicks once.\n\nbench.device('active-buzzer', (part) => {\n  const snd = part.sound();\n  let on = false, volts = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      volts = io.supply('+', '-');\n      const p = io.pwm('+');\n      // driven by tone(): its oscillator gets chopped, which sounds rough (as a real one does)\n      const level = p ? p.duty : 1;\n      on = volts > 2.5 && level > 0.05;\n      if (on) snd.tone(2300, Math.min(1, (volts / 5) * (p ? 0.6 : 0.8)), p ? 'sawtooth' : 'square');\n      else snd.stop();\n      io.draw(on ? 0.025 : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      return [on ? `beeping (${volts.toFixed(1)} V)` : volts > 0.5 ? `quiet (${volts.toFixed(1)} V is too little)` : 'quiet'];\n    },\n  };\n});\n\nbench.device('passive-buzzer', (part) => {\n  const snd = part.sound();\n  let hz = 0, volts = 0, clickUntil = -1, lastLevel = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      const p = io.pwm('+');\n      volts = (io.v('+') ?? 0) - (io.v('-') ?? 0);\n      const level = io.level('+') ?? 0;\n      if (p && p.hz >= 20 && volts > 0.5) {\n        hz = p.hz;\n        snd.tone(hz, Math.min(1, volts / 5) * Math.min(1, p.duty * 2), 'square');\n      } else {\n        hz = 0;\n        // a steady level only moves its disc once: a click\n        if (level !== lastLevel) clickUntil = io.time + 0.01;\n        if (io.time < clickUntil) snd.tone(180, 0.3, 'square');\n        else snd.stop();\n      }\n      lastLevel = level;\n      io.draw(hz ? 0.015 : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      return [hz ? `playing ${Math.round(hz)} Hz` : 'quiet (it needs tone(pin, frequency))'];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","parts":[{"id":"active-buzzer","name":"Active buzzer","description":"Beeps (about 2.3 kHz) whenever + is above 2.5 V: digitalWrite(pin, HIGH) to beep, LOW to stop. Long leg + to a pin, short leg - to GND. A tone() on it just sounds rough: it has its own oscillator.","swatch":"#1c1c1e","mass":2,"sound":true,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.6,0.9],"at":[0,0.45,0],"color":"#1c1c1e"},{"cyl":[0.12,0.02],"at":[0,0.91,0],"color":"#0a0a0a","collide":false},{"box":[0.5,0.01,0.12],"at":[0,0.905,-0.3],"color":"#f2f2f2","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"+","label":"+ (long leg)","at":[-0.25,0,0],"kind":"in"},{"id":"-","label":"- (short leg)","at":[0.25,0,0],"kind":"gnd"}],"device":"active-buzzer"},{"id":"passive-buzzer","name":"Passive buzzer","description":"Plays the frequency it's driven at: tone(pin, 440) is an A, noTone(pin) stops. A plain HIGH only clicks. + to a pin, - to GND.","swatch":"#14361f","mass":2,"sound":true,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.6,0.8],"at":[0,0.4,0],"color":"#1c1c1e"},{"box":[1.3,0.08,1.3],"at":[0,0.04,0],"color":"#1d6b3a"},{"cyl":[0.15,0.02],"at":[0,0.81,0],"color":"#0a0a0a","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"+","label":"+ (signal)","at":[-0.25,0,0],"kind":"in"},{"id":"-","label":"-","at":[0.25,0,0],"kind":"gnd"}],"device":"passive-buzzer"}],"examples":[{"name":"Play a tune","description":"A board playing a short tune on a passive buzzer with tone(), and beeping an active buzzer between the notes. Press Run (and turn Sound on).","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Play a tune","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"pz","type":"buzzers/passive-buzzer","name":"Passive buzzer","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[6,0,-2],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"az","type":"buzzers/active-buzzer","name":"Active buzzer","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[6,0,2],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"pz","pin":"+"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"pz","pin":"-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP14"},"b":{"uid":"az","pin":"+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"az","pin":"-"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// A tune on the passive buzzer (tone plays a frequency), a beep on the active one between rounds.\n#define BUZZER 15\n#define BEEPER 14\n\nint melody[] = {262, 294, 330, 349, 392, 392, 440, 440, 392};\nint beats[]  = {1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 4};\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(BEEPER, OUTPUT);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  for (int i = 0; i < 9; i++) {\n    Serial.print(\"note \");\n    Serial.println(melody[i]);\n    tone(BUZZER, melody[i], beats[i] * 150);\n    delay(beats[i] * 200);\n  }\n  digitalWrite(BEEPER, HIGH);\n  delay(300);\n  digitalWrite(BEEPER, LOW);\n  delay(1000);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}